From 0722f1490c09099647a8799dfc4562e146bbeeb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:35:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/57] hw/sensor, hw/misc, hw/adc: PyKit sensors, RNBD451, SAM
 D5x ADC

ICM-20948 (accelerometer, gyroscope, temperature, the AK09916 through the
auxiliary I2C master's SLV0/SLV4) on the Ruler at 69h; BNO085 (SH-2 over
SHTP: reset, product ID, Set Feature, accelerometer, gyroscope,
magnetometer and rotation-vector reports) as the machine option
bno085=on, the breakout the kit on the desk carries. RNBD451 BLE module
as a chardev on SERCOM2 with its reset on PA14; command replies as read
from the kit (V1.0.0.10), a central for front ends ("connected",
"central-rx", "central-tx"). ADC U2500: instant conversions of the pins
("ain"), scaled supplies, bandgap and the temperature sensor against the
TEMP_LOG calibration. SERCOM I2C host: a clear of SB right after a
smart-mode DATA read no longer swallows the next byte's SB (ASF4 does
that; the next byte arrives at once on the twin). The kit's own
robot-arm code.py runs on the twin.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
